{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "f02e4457-a823-4c7c-ac0e-0449291ccde2",
    "name": "Race Chaos Index API",
    "description": "DTSC 3601 Homework 4 -- Race Chaos Index API.\n\nScores a single Formula 1 race's results plus neutralization counts for how 'chaotic' (directionally eventful) and 'weird' (non-directionally unusual, via IsolationForest) it was, relative to ~185 historical races (2018-2026). Backed by a fitted scikit-learn Pipeline (custom RaceChaosFeaturizer -> QuantileTransformer -> IsolationForest) loaded once at import time -- not rebuilt on each request.\n\nSet the collection variable `baseUrl` to the deployed Modal URL (e.g. https://sirjacket42--race-chaos-index-fastapi-app.modal.run) before running. Never point this collection at localhost -- the assignment requires assertions against the live deployed API. Modal cold starts can take a few seconds on the first request after idling; if a request times out, increase the request timeout in Postman settings or run it again.\n\nRun order: Health -> Pipeline info -> Score race (valid) -> Score race (invalid). Each request's Tests tab asserts status code and response shape.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "https://sirjacket42--race-chaos-index-fastapi-app.modal.run",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "health"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Liveness/readiness check. Returns 200 with {\"status\": \"ok\", \"model_loaded\": true} once the pipeline.joblib bundle has loaded successfully at import time; the dependency raises 503 (not 500) if the artifact failed to load."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status code is 200', function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test('status is ok', function () {",
              "    const json = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.expect(json.status).to.eql('ok');",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test('model_loaded is true', function () {",
              "    const json = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.expect(json.model_loaded).to.eql(true);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Pipeline info",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/info",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "info"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Describes the loaded artifact: pipeline step names + classes, build metadata (sklearn/numpy/python versions, built_at, training set size/seasons), feature descriptions, chaos label thresholds, and an example request body. Proves the served pipeline has learned state (a rebuilt-at-boot pipeline would not carry a meaningful built_at/training history)."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status code is 200', function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "",
              "const json = pm.response.json();",
              "",
              "pm.test('metadata.steps is an array with at least 3 steps', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(json.metadata).to.have.property('steps');",
              "    pm.expect(json.metadata.steps).to.be.an('array');",
              "    pm.expect(json.metadata.steps.length).to.be.at.least(3);",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test('metadata.sklearn_version and built_at are non-empty strings', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(json.metadata.sklearn_version).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
              "    pm.expect(json.metadata.built_at).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test('includes the RaceChaosFeaturizer step', function () {",
              "    const hasFeaturizer = json.metadata.steps.some(",
              "        (step) => step.class && step.class.includes('RaceChaosFeaturizer')",
              "    );",
              "    pm.expect(hasFeaturizer).to.be.true;",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
